Here is one of many possible ways to
create separate data frames, based on whether the entry in a column appears
more than once or not.  This one uses table()to count how often the
items in x appear:

 

> tbl <- table(x)

> is.dupe <- tbl[x]>1

> dupeRows <- xy[is.dupe,]

> uniqueRows <- xy[not(is.dupe),]

> dupeRows

  x y 

1 a 1

2 a 2

3 b 3

4 b 4

5 c 5

6 c 6

7 c 7

> uniqueRows

   x  y 

 8 d  8

 9 e  9

10 f 10

> 

 

